    "permuted_edges": "Seed 147 permutes directed edges with their corresponding periodic offsets.",
    "permuted_atoms": "Seed 147 relabels atom rows and both edge indices, then restores the force ordering.",
    "contributions": "A zero-valued, differentiable scalar perturbation per input row at one dense weight entry gives per-row mixed derivatives of the full energy-plus-force loss. Summing these terms reconstructs that weight gradient in FP64.",
    "native_intervals": "For two same-order eager results x and y with tolerances tx=atol+rtol*abs(x) and ty for y, the smallest possible maximum error ratio of any fixed value against both is abs(x-y)/(tx+ty). A value above one proves their two permitted intervals do not intersect.",
